Step 3: Login to ArgoCD via UI
Go to the ArgoCD web interface.
Use the following credentials:
Username: admin
Password: Run the following command to fetch the password:
cat /root/lab-data/argocd-password
Step 4: Create an ArgoCD Application
In the UI, create a new application with the following details:
App Name: solar-system-app
Project: default
Sync Policy: Manual
Sync Options: ENABLE Auto-create Namespace
Repo URL: Go to the Gitea UI and retrieve the URL
Revision: main
Path: ./kubernetes
Cluster: https://kubernetes.default.svc
Namespace: solar-system
Save the application.
Step 5: Sync the Application Manually
After saving, manually sync the application from the ArgoCD interface.
Step 6: Verify Sync Status
The sync will succeed, but the ArgoCD app status will be degraded because the Docker image may not be available at your DockerHub.

================================================================================================
Step 1: Generate a Gitea Token
Generate a Gitea token from the Gitea UI:
Go to User profile (top-right) -> Settings -> Applications.
Token name: Jenkins-Token
Select permission: Repository Read and Write
Copy the generated token for future use.
Step 2: Create Jenkins Global Credentials
In Jenkins, create new Global Credentials:
Kind: Secret text
Scope: Global
Secret: Paste the token you generated from Gitea
ID: gitea-api-token
Step 3: Update Jenkinsfile
In the Jenkinsfile, add the gitea-api-token as a global environment variable:
GITEA_TOKEN = credentials('gitea-api-token')
Add the following two stages in Jenkins after Integration Testing - VM stage. Replace the *docker image name.
stage('Update and Commit Image Tag') {
    when  {
            branch 'PR*'
          }
    steps {
        sh 'git clone -b main http://git-server:5555/dasher-org/solar-system-gitops-argocd'
        dir("solar-system-gitops-argocd/kubernetes") {
            sh '''
                git checkout main
                git checkout -b feature-$BUILD_ID
                sed -i "s#kodekloud-hub:5000.*#kodekloud-hub:5000/solar-system:$GIT_COMMIT#g" deployment.yml
                cat deployment.yml
                git config user.name "Jenkins CI"
                git config --global user.email "jenkins@dasher.com"
                git remote set-url origin http://$GITEA_TOKEN@git-server:5555/dasher-org/solar-system-gitops-argocd
                git add .
                git commit -am "Updated docker image"
                git push -u origin feature-$BUILD_ID
            '''
        }
    }
}
stage('Kubernetes Deployment - Raise PR') {
    when  {
            branch 'PR*'
           }
    steps {
        sh """
          curl -X 'POST' \
            'http://git-server:5555/api/v1/repos/dasher-org/solar-system-gitops-argocd/pulls' \
            -H 'accept: application/json' \
            -H 'Authorization: token $GITEA_TOKEN' \
            -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
            -d '{
            "assignee": "gitea-admin",
            "assignees": [
              "gitea-admin"
            ],
            "base": "main",
            "body": "Updated docker image in deployment manifest",
            "head": "feature-$BUILD_ID",
            "title": "Updated Docker Image"
          }'
        """
    }
}
Add the contents of /root/lab-data/q11-data-2.txt at the top of the post always section:
script {
            if (fileExists('solar-system-gitops-argocd')) {
            sh 'rm -rf solar-system-gitops-argocd'
            }
        }
Step 4: Commit Changes and Open a PR
Commit the changes to the Jenkinsfile in the feature/enabling-cicd branch.
Open a Pull Request from the feature/enabling-cicd branch to the main branch.
Once the PR is opened, Jenkins will trigger the pipeline.
NOTE: Do not merge or close the PR in the solar-system repository.

Step 5: Accept and Merge the PR
Switch to Gitea, go to the solar-system-gitops-argocd repository.
Notice the Pull Request.
Accept and merge it.
Step 6: Sync the Application in ArgoCD
Switch to the ArgoCD UI.
Refresh the solar-system-app.
Manually sync the application.
Check the Kubernetes app on port 30000.
